## 🎯 Overview

**FinSentiment** is an end-to-end machine learning system designed to classify financial news headlines into three sentiment categories: **Positive**, **Negative**, and **Neutral**. It combines a fine-tuned **FinBERT** transformer model with a robust **Django REST API** backend and a modern **Next.js** frontend.

### Why This Project?

Financial markets react instantly to news. Traders, analysts, and fintech applications need to process thousands of headlines per day to gauge market mood. Manual analysis is impossible at scale — this project automates it with **95.35% accuracy** and **sub-200ms latency**.

### What Makes It Different?

- 🎯 **Domain-Specific Model** — Fine-tuned on 77K+ financial sentences, not generic sentiment data
- ⚡ **Production-Ready** — Docker, PostgreSQL, Redis, and WebSocket support out of the box
- 📊 **Full-Stack Solution** — From training notebook to deployed web application
- 🔌 **Developer-Friendly** — Clean REST API, real-time WebSocket streaming, and batch processing

---

## ✨ Features

### Core Capabilities

| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| 🧠 **Fine-Tuned FinBERT** | Domain-adapted transformer for financial text (95.35% accuracy) |
| ⚡ **Real-Time Prediction** | Sub-200ms response time on CPU inference |
| 📊 **3-Way Classification** | Positive / Negative / Neutral with calibrated confidence scores |
| 🔌 **REST API** | Simple JSON endpoints for seamless integration |
| 🌐 **WebSocket Streaming** | Push-based real-time sentiment updates |
| 📈 **Analytics Dashboard** | Interactive charts for trend analysis |
| 💾 **PostgreSQL Persistence** | Every prediction stored for historical analysis |
| 📦 **Batch Processing** | Analyze thousands of headlines in a single request |
| 🐳 **Dockerized** | One-command deployment with `docker-compose up` |
| 🎨 **Modern UI** | Glassmorphism design with Framer Motion animations |

